-- W67 (O12, M14): a `case` nested in the fall-through branch of the one before
-- it, 500 deep — twice the length that exceeded the host parser's
-- nesting (250). The inner `case` is the body of a branch that binds
-- nothing (or binds a variable the inner does not mention), so it floats
-- out as a binding forced when the branch is taken; the scrutinees are
-- evaluated in order, exactly as GHC. Pinned against GHC: first, middle,
-- last and fall-through, for literal and for constructor patterns.

